 ## Recent releases
 
-### v1.4.1 — current stable (November 9, 2026)
+### v1.5.0 — current stable (November 10, 2026)
+
+- **Guardrails as code**: a versioned, layered policy that agents cannot get around, enforced in task worktrees too; every tool result is scanned for prompt injection before the agent reads it
+- **Red team**: after QA, an agent tries to break what the task built, judged by WorkPilot's own run
+- **Plan rehearsal** replays a spec's plan over the base branch before the build; the **migration guard** reviews a task's migrations for data loss, renames, NOT NULL without default and locks, on every stack
+- **Quality agents for every stack**: accessibility (WCAG 2.2 score per criterion and page, dynamic scan), i18n (key proposals, plurals, RTL), API contract watcher (against the target branch, consumers, QA gate), doc drift, flaky tests (cause and fix card), compliance evidence, onboarding story per role; fixes go on a review branch
+- **Release Train** deploys the services of an approved train file in dependency order, with health and smoke checks, a click per production service and cascading rollback
+- **Git history surgeon**: squash, reword and split a branch's commits onto a new branch with the same code, never pushed
+- **Best-of-N arbiter** when variants do not do the same thing; **carbon budget** per month with an ESG export; **production incidents** (Sentry or an inbox) become bug-fix cards
+- **Notebooks**: cell dependencies, runs in a fresh kernel without credentials, long cells turned into functions on a review card
+- **Personal coach**: your coding style per language, learned from your git history and lint config, given to the coder and QA fixer; editable and exportable
+- **Fixes**: the release builds on the tag again, « Install SOUL.md » in the packaged app; **security**: deepmerge patched in the mobile app
+
+### v1.4.1 — November 9, 2026
 
 - **Every write goes through review**: the test generation studio, Import Design, the changelog, pair programming and the Kanban quick command write on the branch of a « Generated code » card in Human Review; you read the diff, then « Create PR »
 - **A lighter left menu**: a rail of spaces with one panel at a time, « My menu » for pinned and recent pages, the Toolbox in four hubs (20 entries become 9), the 14 beta pages in a **Labo**, an offer to hide pages unused for 30 days; Ctrl+K and `/` find all 77 pages by name, group or keyword
